WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.720
Nitrogen and oxygen make
up 99 per cent of dry air.

2
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.260
Carbon dioxide is only
a trace: at Mauna Loa,

3
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:16.830
about 421 parts per million in
2023, up from about 316 in 1959.

4
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.690
Earth's warm surface glows in infrared.

5
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:24.590
These rare molecules absorb it;
the nitrogen and oxygen don't.

6
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.590
Why do a few rare molecules
catch the infrared,

7
00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.480
while the rest of the air lets it pass?

8
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.610
In this mission, you'll meet
the main greenhouse gases,

9
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.080
and their natural and human sources.

10
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.080
Then you'll follow the
energy a molecule absorbs,

11
00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:41.970
and see why some heads back down.

12
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:47.670
Your mission: explain why carbon dioxide
and water vapour absorb Earth's infrared,

13
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.950
but nitrogen and oxygen don't.
